= Struct


// OVERVIEW SECTION STARTS
[#overview]
--

[float]
=== Description
The `struct` keyword is used to create a structure type to group several related variables into one place. The variables inside the struct are called member of the structure

A structure can contain many variables with different data types.
[%hardbreaks]
[float]
=== Creating (Declaring) a struct

All of the methods below are valid ways to create (declare) a struct.
[source,arduino]
----
  // Declare an struct with the type name myStruct:
  struct myStruct {
    string myString;
    int myInt;
  };

  // Declare an struct with the type name myStruct and the instance name myStruct1:
  struct myStruct {
    string myString;
    int myInt;
  } myStruct1;

 
----

